{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PQxMgUCwxsaqw3mRL7n518","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tschema_version: 1\n3\tkind: delivery-intent\n4\tid: DI-RATE-LIMIT\n5\ttitle: Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\n6\tclaim: proposed\n7\tsource:\n8\t  uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n9\t  captured_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00Z'\n10\t  sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\n11\tsuccess:\n12\t- A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n13\t- Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n14\t- Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n15\t- The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\n16\tout_of_scope:\n17\t- Replacing provider-owned usage metering.\n18\t- Choosing production storage or deployment infrastructure.\n19\t---\n20\t# Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\n21\t\n22\t## Delivery outcome\n23\t\n24\tFor every organization request, resolve one effective rate-limit policy, deny request 101 when the effective limit is 100, and expose a stable reason plus decision telemetry without changing provider-owned metering.\n25\t\n26\t## Evidence boundary\n27\t\n28\tThis artifact records a **proposed** claim. Its source, capture time,\n29\tand content hash are recorded in frontmatter; the claim is not implementation\n30\tevidence by itself.\n31\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b50dc51b-759e-4144-823c-3edbcc3e51c7","uuid":"ddfb944d-f196-48cd-bb48-31635df7e382","timestamp":"2026-09-15T11:05:21.102Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/zf/r0gsd5px2v9_q24j3tfnyb5c0000gn/T/taskspec chat bro7v3pn/tasks/.plans/rate-limit/intent.md","content":"---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: delivery-intent\nid: DI-RATE-LIMIT\ntitle: Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\nclaim: proposed\nsource:\n  uri: tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n  captured_at: '2026-08-02T00:00:00Z'\n  sha256: f40ed16c2898b8363dfce1c19e7c3fd539d52810d52b21faeaf59323117af445\nsuccess:\n- A versioned policy schema rejects invalid limits and windows.\n- Resolution produces exactly one effective policy for an organization.\n- Request 101 is denied after 100 allowed requests in the same window.\n- The denial returns a stable reason and emits matching decision telemetry.\nout_of_scope:\n- Replacing provider-owned usage metering.\n- Choosing production storage or deployment infrastructure.\n---\n# Enforce organization-level request limits with visible decisions\n\n## Delivery outcome\n\nFor every organization request, resolve one effective rate-limit policy, deny request 101 when the effective limit is 100, and expose a stable reason plus decision telemetry without changing provider-owned metering.\n\n## Evidence boundary\n\nThis artifact records a **proposed** claim. Its source, capture time,\nand content hash are recorded in frontmatter; the claim is not implementation\nevidence by itself.\n","numLines":31,"startLine":1,"totalLines":31}}}
