{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B37vEJvX8SisUdscanU8nj","type":"tool_result","content":"======================================================================\nT-20260802-policy-schema | Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema | effort: S | profile: standard | backend: any\nGOAL: Give every downstream stage one validated policy contract.\nWHY: Give every downstream stage one validated policy contract.\nDONE: A JSON Schema accepts valid limits and windows and rejects invalid values.\nCREATES: ['src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json', 'tests/test_policy_schema.py']\nTOUCHES: []\nDO_NOT_TOUCH: ['tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md']\nOBS: \"policy schema test pass count\"\nROLLBACK: Remove the additive schema and its focused tests.\nSOURCE_NOTE: tasks/.plans/rate-limit/legs/LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID.md#T-20260802-policy-schema\nBEHAVIORS: [{\"given\": \"a policy with a positive limit and window\", \"id\": \"B-1\", \"then\": \"schema validation succeeds\", \"when\": \"the document is validated\"}, {\"given\": \"a policy with a zero limit or window\", \"id\": \"B-2\", \"then\": \"schema validation fails\", \"when\": \"the document is validated\"}]\nPROVENANCE: {\"contract\": \"TaskPlanProvenance/v1\", \"initiative\": \"rate-limit\", \"projection_digest\": \"5e6880a656be7cea80e5b6e4d881764fa82dcd46e456e34ebdf9f015ca910eda\", \"snapshot\": \"tasks/.plans/rate-limit/snapshots/7d54f2d6eac947ed1d8ebefe76cc2086f29ccd4cf1f48e4dc9bcf95833fa3fbf.json\", \"snapshot_digest\": \"7d54f2d6eac947ed1d8ebefe76cc2086f29ccd4cf1f48e4dc9bcf95833fa3fbf\"}\n======================================================================\nT-20260802-effective-policy | Resolve one effective organization policy | effort: S | profile: standard | backend: any\nGOAL: Make policy precedence explicit before request enforcement.\nWHY: Make policy precedence explicit before request enforcement.\nDONE: The resolver returns one stable policy and provenance for every tested input.\nCREATES: ['src/rate_limit/policy.py', 'tests/test_policy_resolution.py']\nTOUCHES: []\nDO_NOT_TOUCH: ['tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md']\nOBS: \"effective policy resolution test pass count\"\nROLLBACK: Remove the additive resolver and focused tests.\nSOURCE_NOTE: tasks/.plans/rate-limit/legs/LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED.md#T-20260802-effective-policy\nBEHAVIORS: [{\"given\": \"a valid organization override\", \"id\": \"B-1\", \"then\": \"the override and its provenance are returned\", \"when\": \"effective policy is resolved\"}, {\"given\": \"no organization override\", \"id\": \"B-2\", \"then\": \"the validated default and its provenance are returned\", \"when\": \"effective policy is resolved\"}]\nPROVENANCE: {\"contract\": \"TaskPlanProvenance/v1\", \"initiative\": \"rate-limit\", \"projection_digest\": \"cfcef37b5819bd957fb918250a9c73bb0ce5f9900d0bac24090b951d024f8b91\", \"snapshot\": \"tasks/.plans/rate-limit/snapshots/7d54f2d6eac947ed1d8ebefe76cc2086f29ccd4cf1f48e4dc9bcf95833fa3fbf.json\", \"snapshot_digest\": \"7d54f2d6eac947ed1d8ebefe76cc2086f29ccd4cf1f48e4dc9bcf95833fa3fbf\"}\n======================================================================\nT-20260802-request-101 | Enforce the effective limit at request 101 | effort: S | profile: standard | backend: any\nGOAL: Apply one effective policy at the request boundary without off-by-one drift.\nWHY: Apply one effective policy at the request boundary without off-by-one drift.\nDONE: Requests 1-100 are allowed and request 101 is denied for the same organization window.\nCREATES: ['src/rate_limit/enforcement.py', 'tests/test_request_101.py']\nTOUCHES: []\nDO_NOT_TOUCH: ['tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md']\nOBS: \"boundary test pass count\"\nROLLBACK: Remove the additive enforcement boundary and focused tests.\nSOURCE_NOTE: tasks/.plans/rate-limit/legs/LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED.md#T-20260802-request-101\nBEHAVIORS: [{\"given\": \"an effective limit of 100 and count 99\", \"id\": \"B-1\", \"then\": \"the request is allowed\", \"when\": \"request 100 is evaluated\"}, {\"given\": \"an effective limit of 100 and count 100\", \"id\": \"B-2\", \"then\": \"the request is denied exactly once\", \"when\": \"request 101 is evaluated\"}]\nPROVENANCE: {\"contract\": \"TaskPlanProvenance/v1\", \"initiative\": \"rate-limit\", \"projection_digest\": \"f26e32c4369ac5aa22db0c5e9cb4b081f7605cc56fed3fd4fa18305db3287cd0\", \"snapshot\": \"tasks/.plans/rate-limit/snapshots/7d54f2d6eac947ed1d8ebefe76cc2086f29ccd4cf1f48e4dc9bcf95833fa3fbf.json\", \"snapshot_digest\": \"7d54f2d6eac947ed1d8ebefe76cc2086f29ccd4cf1f48e4dc9bcf95833fa3fbf\"}\n======================================================================\nT-20260802-decision-visibility | Expose the denial reason and decision telemetry | effort: S | profile: standard | backend: any\nGOAL: Make the request 101 decision explainable without turning telemetry into authority.\nWHY: Make the request 101 decision explainable without turning telemetry into authority.\nDONE: The denial response and telemetry carry the same stable reason and decision identifier.\nCREATES: ['src/rate_limit/decision.py', 'tests/test_decision_visibility.py']\nTOUCHES: []\nDO_NOT_TOUCH: ['tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md']\nOBS: \"response-to-telemetry correlation test pass count\"\nROLLBACK: Remove the additive response adapter, telemetry event, and focused tests.\nSOURCE_NOTE: tasks/.plans/rate-limit/legs/LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE.md#T-20260802-decision-visibility\nBEHAVIORS: [{\"given\": \"request 101 is denied\", \"id\": \"B-1\", \"then\": \"it exposes the stable reason organization_rate_limit_exceeded\", \"when\": \"the response is created\"}, {\"given\": \"the same denial decision\", \"id\": \"B-2\", \"then\": \"it carries the same reason and decision identifier\", \"when\": \"telemetry is emitted\"}]\nPROVENANCE: {\"contract\": \"TaskPlanProvenance/v1\", \"initiative\": \"rate-limit\", \"projection_digest\": \"3c9e5d17921fcc1d4fe089b2619a6a7b76b1906fb