{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G1CMURoW3oPafmbMQ6VXhi","type":"tool_result","content":"########## seams/SEAM-DECISION-VISIBILITY.md\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-DECISION-VISIBILITY\nname: Decision visibility\ndescription: Separates enforcement from the externally visible reason and observation record.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Present a stable denial reason and emit matching decision telemetry.\nconsumes:\n- allow-or-deny decision\nproduces:\n- visible reason\n- decision telemetry event\nowner: reliability-interface\nindependent_proof: Response and telemetry tests assert the same reason and decision identifier.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Emit a metric without returning a stable reason\n  reason: Callers could not distinguish limit denial from unrelated failures.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-DECISION-VISIBILITY\n  name: Decision visibility lane\n  owner: reliability-interface\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE\n    observable_state: Denials expose a stable reason and matching decision telemetry\n    proof: The response reason and telemetry payload share one decision identifier.\n    requires:\n    - allow-or-deny decision\n    produces:\n    - visible reason\n    - decision telemetry event\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-decision-visibility\n      title: Expose the denial reason and decision telemetry\n      goal: Make the request 101 decision explainable without turning telemetry into authority.\n      done_condition: The denial response and telemetry carry the same stable reason and decision identifier.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on:\n      - T-20260802-request-101\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/decision.py\n      - tests/test_decision_visibility.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: request 101 is denied\n        when: the response is created\n        then: it exposes the stable reason organization_rate_limit_exceeded\n      - id: B-2\n        given: the same denial decision\n        when: telemetry is emitted\n        then: it carries the same reason and decision identifier\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: The response exposes the stable denial reason\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k response_reason\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Telemetry carries the matching reason\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k telemetry_reason\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: Response and telemetry share a decision identifier\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k decision_identifier\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: expose an unstable free-text reason\n        reason: clients and operators could not depend on it\n        instead: use a stable machine reason plus human detail\n      - action: let telemetry authorize the denial\n        reason: observation cannot cross the enforcement boundary\n        instead: emit only after receiving the decision\n      - action: omit decision lineage\n        reason: response and telemetry could not be correlated\n        instead: carry one decision identifier across both outputs\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive response adapter, telemetry event, and focused tests.\n      observability: response-to-telemetry correlation test pass count\n---\n# Decision visibility\n\nSeparates enforcement from the externally visible reason and observation record.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nPresent a stable denial reason and emit matching decision telemetry.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nResponse and telemetry tests assert the same reason and decision identifier.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Emit a metric without returning a stable reason** — Callers could not distinguish limit denial from unrelated failures.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.\n########## seams/SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT.md\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT\nname: Policy contract\ndescription: Separates accepted policy shape from resolution and enforcement.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Define and validate versioned organization rate-limit policy data.\nconsumes:\n- authored organization policy\nproduces:\n- validated policy document\nowner: platform-contracts\nindependent_proof: Invalid limits and windows fail schema validation deterministically.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Treat the API handler as the policy boundary\n  reason: Handler ownership would mix contract, resolution, and enforcement concerns.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-POLICY-CONTRACT\n  name: Policy contract lane\n  owner: platform-contracts\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID\n    observable_state: Rate-limit policy documents are schema-valid\n    proof: Invalid limits and windows are rejected; required fields are machine-readable.\n    requires: []\n    produces:\n    - validated policy document\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-policy-schema\n      title: Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema\n      goal: Give every downstream stage one validated policy contract.\n      done_condition: A JSON Schema accepts valid limits and windows and rejects invalid values.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on: []\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json\n      - tests/test_policy_schema.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: a policy with a positive limit and window\n        when: the document is validated\n        then: schema validation succeeds\n      - id: B-2\n        given: a policy with a zero limit or window\n        when: the document is validated\n        then: schema validation fails\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: The policy schema exists and parses as JSON\n        bash: test -f src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json && python3 -m json.tool src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json\n          >/dev/null\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Valid policy examples pass the schema tests\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_schema.py -k valid\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: Invalid non-positive values are rejected\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_schema.py -k invalid\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: encode limits only in handler constants\n        reason: downstream resolution would have no versioned contract\n        instead: validate one explicit schema before resolution\n      - action: accept zero or negative windows\n        reason: enforcement semantics would be undefined\n        instead: reject non-positive values at the contract boundary\n      - action: couple the schema to one storage provider\n        reason: policy shape and persistence are separate decisions\n        instead: keep the schema provider-neutral\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive schema and its focused tests.\n      observability: policy schema test pass count\n---\n# Policy contract\n\nSeparates accepted policy shape from resolution and enforcement.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nDefine and validate versioned organization rate-limit policy data.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nInvalid limits and windows fail schema validation deterministically.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Treat the API handler as the policy boundary** — Handler ownership would mix contract, resolution, and enforcement concerns.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.\n########## seams/SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION.md\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION\nname: Effective policy resolution\ndescription: Separates policy precedence from request-time enforcement.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Resolve exactly one effective policy from validated inputs.\nconsumes:\n- validated policy document\n- organization identity\nproduces:\n- effective policy decision\nowner: policy-runtime\nindependent_proof: A deterministic precedence suite returns one effective policy.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Resolve policy independently inside every request adapter\n  reason: Multiple precedence implementations would drift and become unprovable.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-POLICY-RESOLUTION\n  name: Effective policy lane\n  owner: policy-runtime\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED\n    observable_state: Every organization has one effective policy decision\n    proof: Defaults and organization overrides resolve with deterministic precedence.\n    requires:\n    - validated policy document\n    produces:\n    - effective policy decision\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-effective-policy\n      title: Resolve one effective organization policy\n      goal: Make policy precedence explicit before request enforcement.\n      done_condition: The resolver returns one stable policy and provenance for every tested input.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on:\n      - T-20260802-policy-schema\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/policy.py\n      - tests/test_policy_resolution.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: a valid organization override\n        when: effective policy is resolved\n        then: the override and its provenance are returned\n      - id: B-2\n        given: no organization override\n        when: effective policy is resolved\n        then: the validated default and its provenance are returned\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: Organization overrides win deterministically\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k override\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Defaults resolve when no override exists\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k default\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: Resolution returns policy provenance\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k provenance\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: hide precedence inside conditional request code\n        reason: effective policy would not be independently testable\n        instead: expose one deterministic resolver\n      - action: return a policy without provenance\n        reason: operators could not explain the enforcement decision\n        instead: return source and version with the policy\n      - action: silently invent a default\n        reason: missing policy is an ownership decision\n        instead: require a validated explicit default\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive resolver and focused tests.\n      observability: effective policy resolution test pass count\n---\n# Effective policy resolution\n\nSeparates policy precedence from request-time enforcement.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nResolve exactly one effective policy from validated inputs.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nA deterministic precedence suite returns one effective policy.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Resolve policy independently inside every request adapter** — Multiple precedence implementations would drift and become unprovable.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.\n########## seams/SEAM-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT.md\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\nname: Request enforcement\ndescription: Separates the allow-or-deny decision from response presentation and telemetry.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Apply the effective policy to the organization request count.\nconsumes:\n- effective policy decision\n- organization identity\n- current request count\nproduces:\n- allow-or-deny decision\nowner: request-runtime\nindependent_proof: A boundary test allows requests 1 through 100 and denies request 101.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Infer enforcement from emitted metrics\n  reason: Telemetry observes a decision but cannot authorize or make it.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\n  name: Request enforcement lane\n  owner: request-runtime\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED\n    observable_state: Request 101 is denied for a limit of 100\n    proof: Boundary tests allow the first 100 requests and deny the next request once.\n    requires:\n    - effective policy decision\n    produces:\n    - allow-or-deny decision\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-request-101\n      title: Enforce the effective limit at request 101\n      goal: Apply one effective policy at the request boundary without off-by-one drift.\n      done_condition: Requests 1-100 are allowed and request 101 is denied for the same organization window.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on:\n      - T-20260802-effective-policy\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/enforcement.py\n      - tests/test_request_101.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: an effective limit of 100 and count 99\n        when: request 100 is evaluated\n        then: the request is allowed\n      - id: B-2\n        given: an effective limit of 100 and count 100\n        when: request 101 is evaluated\n        then: the request is denied exactly once\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: Request 100 remains allowed\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k request_100\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Request 101 is denied\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k request_101\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: The boundary has no off-by-one drift\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k boundary\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: check the limit after allowing the request\n        reason: request 101 would pass through\n        instead: decide before forwarding work\n      - action: use telemetry as the enforcement source\n        reason: observation is not authorization\n        instead: return an explicit decision from enforcement\n      - action: share counters across organizations\n        reason: one tenant could consume another tenant's budget\n        instead: key state by organization and window\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive enforcement boundary and focused tests.\n      observability: boundary test pass count\n---\n# Request enforcement\n\nSeparates the allow-or-deny decision from response presentation and telemetry.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nApply the effective policy to the organization request count.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nA boundary test allows requests 1 through 100 and denies request 101.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Infer enforcement from emitted metrics** — Telemetry observes a decision but cannot authorize or make it.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b50dc51b-759e-4144-823c-3edbcc3e51c7","uuid":"4b0d6607-6c91-4390-8cc3-4dbf00b047d7","timestamp":"2026-09-15T11:05:55.208Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"########## seams/SEAM-DECISION-VISIBILITY.md\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-DECISION-VISIBILITY\nname: Decision visibility\ndescription: Separates enforcement from the externally visible reason and observation record.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Present a stable denial reason and emit matching decision telemetry.\nconsumes:\n- allow-or-deny decision\nproduces:\n- visible reason\n- decision telemetry event\nowner: reliability-interface\nindependent_proof: Response and telemetry tests assert the same reason and decision identifier.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Emit a metric without returning a stable reason\n  reason: Callers could not distinguish limit denial from unrelated failures.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-DECISION-VISIBILITY\n  name: Decision visibility lane\n  owner: reliability-interface\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-DENIAL-REASON-VISIBLE\n    observable_state: Denials expose a stable reason and matching decision telemetry\n    proof: The response reason and telemetry payload share one decision identifier.\n    requires:\n    - allow-or-deny decision\n    produces:\n    - visible reason\n    - decision telemetry event\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-decision-visibility\n      title: Expose the denial reason and decision telemetry\n      goal: Make the request 101 decision explainable without turning telemetry into authority.\n      done_condition: The denial response and telemetry carry the same stable reason and decision identifier.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on:\n      - T-20260802-request-101\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/decision.py\n      - tests/test_decision_visibility.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: request 101 is denied\n        when: the response is created\n        then: it exposes the stable reason organization_rate_limit_exceeded\n      - id: B-2\n        given: the same denial decision\n        when: telemetry is emitted\n        then: it carries the same reason and decision identifier\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: The response exposes the stable denial reason\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k response_reason\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Telemetry carries the matching reason\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k telemetry_reason\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: Response and telemetry share a decision identifier\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_decision_visibility.py -k decision_identifier\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: expose an unstable free-text reason\n        reason: clients and operators could not depend on it\n        instead: use a stable machine reason plus human detail\n      - action: let telemetry authorize the denial\n        reason: observation cannot cross the enforcement boundary\n        instead: emit only after receiving the decision\n      - action: omit decision lineage\n        reason: response and telemetry could not be correlated\n        instead: carry one decision identifier across both outputs\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive response adapter, telemetry event, and focused tests.\n      observability: response-to-telemetry correlation test pass count\n---\n# Decision visibility\n\nSeparates enforcement from the externally visible reason and observation record.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nPresent a stable denial reason and emit matching decision telemetry.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nResponse and telemetry tests assert the same reason and decision identifier.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Emit a metric without returning a stable reason** — Callers could not distinguish limit denial from unrelated failures.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.\n########## seams/SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT.md\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-POLICY-CONTRACT\nname: Policy contract\ndescription: Separates accepted policy shape from resolution and enforcement.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Define and validate versioned organization rate-limit policy data.\nconsumes:\n- authored organization policy\nproduces:\n- validated policy document\nowner: platform-contracts\nindependent_proof: Invalid limits and windows fail schema validation deterministically.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Treat the API handler as the policy boundary\n  reason: Handler ownership would mix contract, resolution, and enforcement concerns.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-POLICY-CONTRACT\n  name: Policy contract lane\n  owner: platform-contracts\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-POLICY-SCHEMA-VALID\n    observable_state: Rate-limit policy documents are schema-valid\n    proof: Invalid limits and windows are rejected; required fields are machine-readable.\n    requires: []\n    produces:\n    - validated policy document\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-policy-schema\n      title: Define the versioned rate-limit policy schema\n      goal: Give every downstream stage one validated policy contract.\n      done_condition: A JSON Schema accepts valid limits and windows and rejects invalid values.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on: []\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json\n      - tests/test_policy_schema.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: a policy with a positive limit and window\n        when: the document is validated\n        then: schema validation succeeds\n      - id: B-2\n        given: a policy with a zero limit or window\n        when: the document is validated\n        then: schema validation fails\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: The policy schema exists and parses as JSON\n        bash: test -f src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json && python3 -m json.tool src/rate_limit/policy.schema.json\n          >/dev/null\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Valid policy examples pass the schema tests\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_schema.py -k valid\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: Invalid non-positive values are rejected\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_schema.py -k invalid\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: encode limits only in handler constants\n        reason: downstream resolution would have no versioned contract\n        instead: validate one explicit schema before resolution\n      - action: accept zero or negative windows\n        reason: enforcement semantics would be undefined\n        instead: reject non-positive values at the contract boundary\n      - action: couple the schema to one storage provider\n        reason: policy shape and persistence are separate decisions\n        instead: keep the schema provider-neutral\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive schema and its focused tests.\n      observability: policy schema test pass count\n---\n# Policy contract\n\nSeparates accepted policy shape from resolution and enforcement.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nDefine and validate versioned organization rate-limit policy data.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nInvalid limits and windows fail schema validation deterministically.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Treat the API handler as the policy boundary** — Handler ownership would mix contract, resolution, and enforcement concerns.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.\n########## seams/SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION.md\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-POLICY-RESOLUTION\nname: Effective policy resolution\ndescription: Separates policy precedence from request-time enforcement.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Resolve exactly one effective policy from validated inputs.\nconsumes:\n- validated policy document\n- organization identity\nproduces:\n- effective policy decision\nowner: policy-runtime\nindependent_proof: A deterministic precedence suite returns one effective policy.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Resolve policy independently inside every request adapter\n  reason: Multiple precedence implementations would drift and become unprovable.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-POLICY-RESOLUTION\n  name: Effective policy lane\n  owner: policy-runtime\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-EFFECTIVE-POLICY-RESOLVED\n    observable_state: Every organization has one effective policy decision\n    proof: Defaults and organization overrides resolve with deterministic precedence.\n    requires:\n    - validated policy document\n    produces:\n    - effective policy decision\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-effective-policy\n      title: Resolve one effective organization policy\n      goal: Make policy precedence explicit before request enforcement.\n      done_condition: The resolver returns one stable policy and provenance for every tested input.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on:\n      - T-20260802-policy-schema\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/policy.py\n      - tests/test_policy_resolution.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: a valid organization override\n        when: effective policy is resolved\n        then: the override and its provenance are returned\n      - id: B-2\n        given: no organization override\n        when: effective policy is resolved\n        then: the validated default and its provenance are returned\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: Organization overrides win deterministically\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k override\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Defaults resolve when no override exists\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k default\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: Resolution returns policy provenance\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_policy_resolution.py -k provenance\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: hide precedence inside conditional request code\n        reason: effective policy would not be independently testable\n        instead: expose one deterministic resolver\n      - action: return a policy without provenance\n        reason: operators could not explain the enforcement decision\n        instead: return source and version with the policy\n      - action: silently invent a default\n        reason: missing policy is an ownership decision\n        instead: require a validated explicit default\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive resolver and focused tests.\n      observability: effective policy resolution test pass count\n---\n# Effective policy resolution\n\nSeparates policy precedence from request-time enforcement.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nResolve exactly one effective policy from validated inputs.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nA deterministic precedence suite returns one effective policy.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Resolve policy independently inside every request adapter** — Multiple precedence implementations would drift and become unprovable.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.\n########## seams/SEAM-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT.md\n---\nschema_version: 1\nkind: seam\nclaim: derived\nid: SEAM-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\nname: Request enforcement\ndescription: Separates the allow-or-deny decision from response presentation and telemetry.\nevidence:\n- E-BLUEPRINT\nresponsibility: Apply the effective policy to the organization request count.\nconsumes:\n- effective policy decision\n- organization identity\n- current request count\nproduces:\n- allow-or-deny decision\nowner: request-runtime\nindependent_proof: A boundary test allows requests 1 through 100 and denies request 101.\ndecision_ids:\n- ADR-RATE-LIMIT-ORDER\nrejected_alternatives:\n- alternative: Infer enforcement from emitted metrics\n  reason: Telemetry observes a decision but cannot authorize or make it.\nswimlane:\n  id: LANE-REQUEST-ENFORCEMENT\n  name: Request enforcement lane\n  owner: request-runtime\n  legs:\n  - id: LEG-REQUEST-101-DENIED\n    observable_state: Request 101 is denied for a limit of 100\n    proof: Boundary tests allow the first 100 requests and deny the next request once.\n    requires:\n    - effective policy decision\n    produces:\n    - allow-or-deny decision\n    tasks:\n    - id: T-20260802-request-101\n      title: Enforce the effective limit at request 101\n      goal: Apply one effective policy at the request boundary without off-by-one drift.\n      done_condition: Requests 1-100 are allowed and request 101 is denied for the same organization window.\n      effort: S\n      profile: standard\n      execution_backend: any\n      required_tools:\n      - git\n      - bash\n      - python3\n      - pytest\n      depends_on:\n      - T-20260802-effective-policy\n      touches_paths: []\n      creates_paths:\n      - src/rate_limit/enforcement.py\n      - tests/test_request_101.py\n      behavior:\n      - id: B-1\n        given: an effective limit of 100 and count 99\n        when: request 100 is evaluated\n        then: the request is allowed\n      - id: B-2\n        given: an effective limit of 100 and count 100\n        when: request 101 is evaluated\n        then: the request is denied exactly once\n      evals:\n      - id: eval_1\n        description: Request 100 remains allowed\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k request_100\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n      - id: eval_2\n        description: Request 101 is denied\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k request_101\n        verifies:\n        - B-2\n      - id: eval_3\n        description: The boundary has no off-by-one drift\n        bash: pytest -q tests/test_request_101.py -k boundary\n        verifies:\n        - B-1\n        - B-2\n      anti_patterns:\n      - action: check the limit after allowing the request\n        reason: request 101 would pass through\n        instead: decide before forwarding work\n      - action: use telemetry as the enforcement source\n        reason: observation is not authorization\n        instead: return an explicit decision from enforcement\n      - action: share counters across organizations\n        reason: one tenant could consume another tenant's budget\n        instead: key state by organization and window\n      do_not_touch:\n      - tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md\n      rollback: Remove the additive enforcement boundary and focused tests.\n      observability: boundary test pass count\n---\n# Request enforcement\n\nSeparates the allow-or-deny decision from response presentation and telemetry.\n\n## Responsibility\n\nApply the effective policy to the organization request count.\n\n## Independent proof\n\nA boundary test allows requests 1 through 100 and denies request 101.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **Infer enforcement from emitted metrics** — Telemetry observes a decision but cannot authorize or make it.\n\nThis derived seam is ready only while its cited evidence, named owner, contract,\nand rejected alternatives remain intact.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
